# Migrating Convergence Settings

Basin now configures numerical convergence on solvers and execution limits on
executors. The former criterion facility and abbreviated setters remain
available during Basin 1.x and are scheduled for removal in Basin 2.0.

```rust
let solver =
    GradientDescent::new(1e-3).with_absolute_gradient_tolerance(1e-6);
let result = Executor::from_start(problem, solver, x0)
    .max_iter(50_000)
    .max_cost_evals(100_000)
    .run()?;
```

See each [solver's API documentation](../solvers/) for its tolerance setters
and numerical conventions. The
[`ConfiguredSolver` reference](https://docs.rs/basin/latest/basin/core/convergence/struct.ConfiguredSolver.html)
explains optional tolerance semantics and how checks combine. The
[`Executor` reference](https://docs.rs/basin/latest/basin/core/executor/struct.Executor.html)
documents execution budgets, application stops, and checkpoints.

For a working introduction, see [Getting Started](../getting-started/).
The authoritative signatures and defaults live in the
[API reference](https://docs.rs/basin/latest/basin/).
